{
  "description": "Member rows with 'preserve_queue_on_recursive_reset' keep their member's queue when a schedule with 'reset_queue_at_start' plus 'reset_queue_recursive' resets a sequential playlist group tree. Each tree has its own window and ref suffix. A kept playlist group also keeps its own rotation and the queues of its nested members. A playlist is kept when any marked row leads to it, directly or through a kept playlist group, even if an unmarked row also leads to it. The kept member's slot in the parent rotation is still re-queued. The '_dup' dump marks only the second row. The importer and the in-memory hydrator mark both rows, because they share a member playlist. The '_dup' case leaves 'outer_dup:twice_dup' out of group_members, because that key matches only one of the two rows. The '_ctl' tree marks nothing and resets completely.",
